# Runtime state (machine-specific)
config.json
config.local.json
server/data/

# The folder docker-compose.yml mounts as /music — app state, not source. The
# app writes .mlo/data (config.json with the Soulseek password and the RYM
# cookie, auth.db, playlists.db, slskd.yaml), downloads and trash under it, so
# running the compose template inside the checkout must never put that in a
# commit. Two empty files were committed once this way; nothing else was, and
# this is the line that keeps it that way.
music/

